      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nSPEED-Bench preparation script is migrating from [Nemo Skills](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Skills) to [Nemo Gym](https://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/gym). This PR updates the documentation for the updated preparation script.\n\n## Claims\n\n* New script prepare the splits the same format as the previous script.\n* New v1.1 data still works with vllm bench.\n\n\n## Validation\n\n1. Tried to run the one-liner for downloading the data: `curl -LsSf https://raw.githubusercontent.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Gym/refs/heads/main/benchmarks/speed-bench/prepare.py | python3 - --format raw --config all`: data was created as expected with the same format.\n2. After that, successfully ran the example in the docs: \n```bash\nvllm serve meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct \\\n    --speculative-config $'{\"method\": \"eagle3\",\n    \"num_speculative_tokens\": 3,\n    \"model\": \"nvidia/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct-Eagle3\"}'\n```\n\n```bash\nvllm bench serve \\\n    --model meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct \\\n    --dataset-name speed_bench \\\n    --dataset-path \"<YOUR_DOWNLOADED_PATH>/data/speed_bench\" \\\n    --num-prompts -1\n```\n\n\n\n## Details\n\nSPEED-Bench preparation script is moving repositories, and is going to be maintained only in the Gym repo, hence the documentation update is needed.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [ ] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [X] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [X] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [X] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [X] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
